+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Product deletion currently leaves carts and order read paths dependent on the live product record. A discontinued product must be removable without making existing carts unreadable or historical orders unavailable, while new purchases of that product must be prevented.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Remove deleted-product lines from carts when carts are loaded or recalculated, persist the cleaned cart, and recalculate quantity and totals from the remaining lines.
+- Return 404 when an API attempts to add a deleted product or fetch its v2 public product representation.
+- Make checkout tolerate stale deleted-product cart lines and ensure they are never ordered or charged.
+- Render order-product snapshots from persisted order data even when the corresponding catalog product no longer exists; preserve order totals and status updates.
+- Add regression coverage for product deletion across cart, checkout, order, and product API flows.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `deleted-product-lifecycle`: Safe behavior for deleted catalog products across carts, checkout, product lookup, and historical orders.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+Affected areas include the product management and v2 product APIs, shopping-cart facade/service/populators, checkout/order creation, order read populators and facades, persistence mappings used by cart and order products, and integration tests in `sm-shop`. Existing order-product fields already contain the required historical sku, name, quantity, and charge; the change must stop read paths from requiring a live catalog product.
