+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Make cart lifecycle resilient to deleted products
+
+- [x] 1.1 Trace the cart load, calculation, PUT, multi-add, and checkout paths and implement a shared stale-line cleanup that removes unresolved products, dependent attributes, and recalculates persisted cart totals; verify with focused cart/service tests.
+- [x] 1.2 Reject deleted-product cart additions with the existing API 404 contract and ensure valid products remain unaffected; verify with cart API integration tests.
+- [x] 1.3 Ensure checkout uses the cleaned cart and never creates an order line or charge for a deleted product; verify with a checkout integration test covering a cart with both valid and deleted lines.
+
+## 2. Preserve historical order reads
+
+- [x] 2.1 Update order-product read population so persisted sku, name, quantity, one-time charge, and subtotal are always mapped without a live product, while optional catalog enrichment remains best-effort; verify with unit tests for present and missing products.
+- [x] 2.2 Verify merchant and customer order detail/list reads and order status updates work after product deletion without changing totals; add integration coverage for all affected endpoints.
+
+## 3. Enforce deleted-product lookup behavior
+
+- [x] 3.1 Make `GET /api/v2/product/{sku}` return 404 for deleted products and add a regression test proving another product remains retrievable.
+- [x] 3.2 Run the relevant Maven test modules and OpenSpec validation, fix regressions, and record the final verification commands.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the completed OpenSpec change after implementation and verification.
